<h2 id="header-response-codes">Response Codes <a class="permalink" href="#header-response-codes" aria-hidden="true">¶</a></h2>
<p>(acc. to <a href="https://restfulapi.net/http-status-codes/">https://restfulapi.net/http-status-codes/</a>)</p>
<p>Standard HTTP codes are used.</p>
<h2 id="header-basic-rules">Basic Rules <a class="permalink" href="#header-basic-rules" aria-hidden="true">¶</a></h2>
<h3 id="header-filtering">Filtering <a class="permalink" href="#header-filtering" aria-hidden="true">¶</a></h3>
<p>(<em>acc. to <a href="https://jsonapi.org/format/#fetching-filtering">https://jsonapi.org/format/#fetching-filtering</a></em>)</p>
<p>Each attribute can be used as filter.</p>
<pre><code class="language-http"><span class="hljs-request">GET <span class="hljs-string">...?filter[&lt;attribute&gt;]=&lt;value&gt;</span> HTTP/1.1</span>
<span class="hljs-attribute">Accept</span>: <span class="hljs-string">application/vnd.api+json</span></code></pre>
<p>Multiple filters are combined by logical <em>AND</em>.</p>
<pre><code class="language-http"><span class="hljs-request">GET <span class="hljs-string">...?filter[&lt;attribute1&gt;]=&lt;value1&gt;&amp;filter[&lt;attribute2&gt;]=&lt;value2&gt;</span> HTTP/1.1</span>
<span class="hljs-attribute">Accept</span>: <span class="hljs-string">application/vnd.api+json</span></code></pre>
<p>A list of values is combined by logical <em>OR</em>.</p>
<pre><code class="language-http"><span class="hljs-request">GET <span class="hljs-string">...?filter[&lt;attribute&gt;][in]=&lt;value1&gt;,&lt;value2&gt;</span> HTTP/1.1</span>
<span class="hljs-attribute">Accept</span>: <span class="hljs-string">application/vnd.api+json</span></code></pre>
<p>The use of operators is possible by square brackets <code>[]</code> on the key name. A set of operators is combined by logical <em>AND</em>. Possible operators are <code>gt</code>, <code>lt</code>, <code>gte</code>, <code>lte</code>, <code>like</code> and ‘is’</p>
<pre><code class="language-http"><span class="hljs-request">GET <span class="hljs-string">...?filter[&lt;attribute&gt;][gte]=&lt;value1&gt;&amp;filter[&lt;attribute&gt;][lte]=&lt;value2&gt;</span> HTTP/1.1</span>
<span class="hljs-attribute">Accept</span>: <span class="hljs-string">application/vnd.api+json</span></code></pre>
<h4 id="header-additional">Additional <a class="permalink" href="#header-additional" aria-hidden="true">¶</a></h4>
<p>For sending more than 1kB as filter it is possible to send a JSON object in <code>X-RESTful-filter</code> header. The <code>X-RESTful-filter</code> overwrites <code>GET</code> parameters.</p>
<h3 id="header-sorting">Sorting <a class="permalink" href="#header-sorting" aria-hidden="true">¶</a></h3>
<p>(<em>acc. to <a href="https://jsonapi.org/format/#fetching-sorting">https://jsonapi.org/format/#fetching-sorting</a></em>)</p>
<p>On each attribute the result list can be filtered. (This is important for Pagination.) It is possible to define sort order (<code>asc</code>, <code>desc</code>), where default is <code>asc</code>.</p>
<pre><code class="language-http"><span class="hljs-request">GET <span class="hljs-string">...?sort=&lt;attribute1&gt;,-&lt;attribute2&gt;</span> HTTP/1.1</span>
<span class="hljs-attribute">Accept</span>: <span class="hljs-string">application/vnd.api+json</span></code></pre>
<h3 id="header-pagination">Pagination <a class="permalink" href="#header-pagination" aria-hidden="true">¶</a></h3>
<p>(<em>acc. to <a href="https://jsonapi.org/format/#fetching-pagination">https://jsonapi.org/format/#fetching-pagination</a></em>)</p>
<p>To get a limited number of items per request, pagination can be defined by <code>limit</code> and <code>offset</code> parameter.</p>
<pre><code class="language-http"><span class="hljs-request">GET <span class="hljs-string">...?page[limit]=20</span> HTTP/1.1</span>
<span class="hljs-attribute">Accept</span>: <span class="hljs-string">application/vnd.api+json</span></code></pre>
<pre><code class="language-http"><span class="hljs-request">GET <span class="hljs-string">...?page[limit]=20&amp;page[offset]=40</span> HTTP/1.1</span>
<span class="hljs-attribute">Accept</span>: <span class="hljs-string">application/vnd.api+json</span></code></pre>
<h3 id="header-sparse-fieldsets">Sparse Fieldsets <a class="permalink" href="#header-sparse-fieldsets" aria-hidden="true">¶</a></h3>
<p>(<em>acc. to <a href="https://jsonapi.org/format/#fetching-sparse-fieldsets">https://jsonapi.org/format/#fetching-sparse-fieldsets</a></em>)</p>
<p>Type <code>self</code> refers to the attributes of the object itself.</p>
<pre><code class="language-http"><span class="hljs-request">GET <span class="hljs-string">...?fields[self]=&lt;attribute1&gt;,&lt;attribute2&gt;</span> HTTP/1.1</span>
<span class="hljs-attribute">Accept</span>: <span class="hljs-string">application/vnd.api+json</span></code></pre>
<h3 id="header-inclusion-of-related-resources">Inclusion of Related Resources <a class="permalink" href="#header-inclusion-of-related-resources" aria-hidden="true">¶</a></h3>
